   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);background-color:rgb(255,255,255);border:none;line-height:1.2\">\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Hi all,\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Hope to see you at this week&#39;s D-RUG work session (<strong>Wednesday 3-5PM in Wickson 2124</strong>).  In addition to our normal work and Q&amp;A time, we will have a brief  presentation from Steve Culman on the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">plyr</code> package.  <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">plyr</code> extends and improves to R&#39;s <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline\">apply</code> functions to make it easy to split up, manipulate, and recombine data.\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">See you Wednesday,\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Noam</p>\r\n</div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
